Debug mode highlights both declarators of `declare const first: string, second: number` (the first from `declare`, the second by its bare name, types left plain) and a `declare global` block through `global`.
== args
--debug
input/ambient-mixed.ts
== file input/ambient-mixed.ts
declare const first: string, second: number;

declare global {
  interface Window {
    customProp: boolean;
  }
}
== stdout
«declare const first»: string, «second»: number;

«declare global» {
  interface Window {
    customProp: boolean;
  }
}
== stderr
== exit 0
